# The Gorani release key (commits 39g, 39i; docs/INSTALL.md › Checking a download).
#
# verify.sh / verify.ps1 accept a release only if SHA256SUMS.sig was made by
# a key listed here, for the principal "release@gorani" and the namespace
# "gorani-release" — one line per key:
#
#   release@gorani namespaces="gorani-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAA… gorani release key (CI)
#
# The key signs every release in CI (package.yml › sign), from the Actions
# secret RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY. tools/release/new-key.sh makes it on the
# release manager's machine, sets the secret and writes its line here
# (replacing any older key's); commit the file. Until a line is here, every
# release is refused, and CI refuses to sign with a key not listed here.
#
# Whoever installs compares the fingerprint verify prints with the one the
# release manager gave them in person — a key read from the same place as
# the download proves nothing on its own.
release@gorani namespaces="gorani-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAINTd/A4PIMMSdFUBz2m5HKiuISi2b/RYjVxarnAQUs1M gorani release key (CI), made 2026-10-15
